# Provenance of fixtures/compacted-session.jsonl
#
# The user, assistant and system entries of one real Claude Code session file,
# copied byte-for-byte and in order; the attachment, queue-operation,
# last-prompt, atis-latch and cost-state lines were left out. Made 2026-09-30
# by the probe for the compaction brief: CLI 2.1.281, --model haiku, stream-json
# in and out, cwd /tmp/compact-probe, four short turns, then `/compact` sent as a
# user message, then one more question. So the shapes are the CLI's own for a
# manual compaction: the system/compact_boundary, the isCompactSummary summary,
# the isMeta caveat, the <command-name>/compact</command-name> entry and the
# <local-command-stdout>Compacted</local-command-stdout> entry -- the last two
# carrying no promptSource, which is what keeps them out of a transcript.
# The probe's own words were neutral already; on 2026-11-15, for the public
# release, the one home directory in the summary's transcript path was
# renamed, and nothing else in the file changed.
#
# source: ~/.claude/projects/-tmp-compact-probe/3f0c1f5e-8c1a-4b7e-9a51-0c0ffee00001.jsonl
